### TITLE ###
UpRecallsPreviousEntriesAndDownReturns
### DESCRIPTION ###
The one history feature the editor carries. Entries are supplied by the caller,
oldest first, so persistence stays the caller's problem.
### PROMPT ###
>
### HISTORY ###
first
second
### KEYS ###
up
up
down
enter
### VALUE ###
second
### OUTCOME ###
submitted
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
>‸
--- frame 1 (up) ---
>second‸
--- frame 2 (up) ---
>first‸
--- frame 3 (down) ---
>second‸
--- frame 4 (enter) ---
>second

### TITLE ###
WalkingBackOutOfHistoryRestoresTheDraft
### DESCRIPTION ###
Half-typed input is stashed on the first Up and comes back when Down walks off
the end of the history. Losing it would make Up a keystroke you learn to fear.
### PROMPT ###
>
### HISTORY ###
old
### KEYS ###
"draft"
up
down
enter
### VALUE ###
draft
### OUTCOME ###
submitted
### FRAMES ###
