>‸
--- frame 1 (d) ---
>d‸
--- frame 2 (r) ---
>dr‸
--- frame 3 (a) ---
>dra‸
--- frame 4 (f) ---
>draf‸
--- frame 5 (t) ---
>draft‸
--- frame 6 (up) ---
>old‸
--- frame 7 (down) ---
>draft‸
--- frame 8 (enter) ---
>draft

### TITLE ###
UpMovesWithinTheBufferBeforeReachingForHistory
### DESCRIPTION ###
In a multi-line buffer Up is a cursor move; only from the top line does it
recall. This is the bash/zsh/python behavior and the reason history lives in
the editor rather than above it.
### PROMPT ###
>
### CONT_PROMPT ###
.
### HISTORY ###
recalled
### POLICY ###
never
### KEYS ###
"one"
enter
"two"
up
